<section class="fanfiction">
  <div class="fanfiction-container">
  <div class="fanfiction-masthead">
    <h1>Fanfiction</h1>
    <time>Updated — March 2026</time>
  </div>

  <section class="fanfiction-hero">
    <div>
      <h2>Harry and Hermione<br> fanfiction</h2>
      <p class="fanfiction-hero-text">The best collection of the best Harry and Hermione fanfiction on the internet...</p><br>
    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="fanfiction-body-content">
    <div class="fanfiction-section-label">Writers</div>
    <div class="fanfiction-body-text">
      <p>In the pursuit of visual clarity, what we choose to omit becomes as crucial as what we include. This fundamental principle guides contemporary design thinking.</p>
      <p>The intentional use of empty space - what designers call negative space or white space—creates rhythm, hierarchy, and breathing room within compositions. It allows elements to exist without competing for attention, establishing a visual language that speaks through restraint rather than abundance.</p>
      <a href="/fanfiction/writers" class="btn btn-sm w-25 btn-primary">View Writers</a>
    </div>
    <div class="fanfiction-grid-image">
      <img src="/images/fanfictionpage/writers.jpg" alt="writers">
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fanfiction-quote-section">
    <blockquote>
      "Perfection is achieved not when there is nothing more to add, but when there is nothing left to take away."
    </blockquote>
    <p class="fanfiction-quote-attribution">— Antoine de Saint-Exupéry</p>
  </section>

